# tools/al/ales_catalog_verify_witness.rish -- a whole catalog proven whole, end to end: verify_deep(lm, tree) walks two levels of
# content addresses (ALES238).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES238.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-151716_fill-ales238-lotus-catalog-verify.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/library_manifest.rye (ALES226, verify_library -- the catalog level) - lotus/album_manifest.rye (ALES224,
# open_album_manifest + verify_album -- the record level). Pure composition over both levels' public verify APIs -- no new hash, no new
# frame.
#
# lotus/catalog_verify.rye proves a whole catalog whole, top to bottom. The selftest proves: a catalog whose library manifest, album
# manifests, and bundles all match verifies cleanly (the whole-tree law); a swapped album manifest refuses AlbumDigestMismatch at the
# catalog level (the catalog-tamper law); a single flipped bundle byte two levels down refuses TrackDigestMismatch (the record-tamper
# law); a renamed track refuses TrackNameMismatch (the name law); a dropped album refuses CountMismatch (the count law). A pure
# integrity walk only -- no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_catalog_verify_witness.rish

say "ales-catalog-verify: Language EN — ALES238 proves a whole catalog whole end to end: verify_deep(lm, tree) confirms the catalog level (each album manifest's digest matches the library) and then the record level (each bundle's digest matches its album manifest), so a keeper gets ONE answer for a whole body of work."
say "ales-catalog-verify: Style Radiant — content-addressing composes into a proof of the whole tree; the library digest binds each album manifest, each album manifest binds each bundle, a Merkle check the shape of the catalog itself, never re-hashing a mountain of audio into one number; the whole-tree, catalog-tamper, record-tamper, name, and count laws each proven on metal."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/catalog_verify"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/catalog_verify.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-catalog-verify: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/catalog_verify.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-catalog-verify: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-catalog-verify: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-catalog-verify' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-catalog-verify: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-catalog-verify line"

say "ales-catalog-verify: GREEN — a keeper holds one answer for a whole body of work, whole or broken by name at the level it broke; the Lotus catalog family now proves itself end to end. The next Lotus crux still names who made it — a signed carry (crypto seam) on Keaton's word."
